WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.067
-Hi, bud!
-Hi, how are you?

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.067
-It's so good to see you.
I'm fantastic.

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:04.434
-I know,
and there are people here.

00:00:04.434 --> 00:00:05.868
-Yes! I mean, look at this!
-It's amazing.

00:00:05.868 --> 00:00:07.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Doesn't that sound great?

00:00:07.701 --> 00:00:09.067
-Friday night. Whoo!

00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:10.367
-Yeah.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:10.367 --> 00:00:12.100
-Last time you were here
was right before "Star Wars"

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:13.634
came out.
-"Star Wars."

00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:15.567
-And you were not allowed to
really tell me that you were --

00:00:15.567 --> 00:00:17.100
-Anything! The secrets.
-Yeah.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.734
-You could barely tell me
that you were in "Star Wars."

00:00:18.734 --> 00:00:20.367
-[ Laughs ] I know.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:22.400
-It was nuts.
-That must be so hard. I mean --

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.100
-It was. It was all secret,
but it was so cool.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:26.167
-Did you tell your family?
Did you tell your --

00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:28.000
-I did tell them
that I was in it, yeah.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.000
-Were they excited? Impressed?
-Um...no.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.701
[ Laughter ]
Well, you know, like --

00:00:32.701 --> 00:00:35.634
So, my oldest kid is now 14,
almost 15.

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:37.701
But then, I bet --
I guess he was about 12.

00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:39.667
-12, yeah.
-And I said, you know,

00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:41.968
"River, I'm --
you know, I'm in 'Star Wars,'

00:00:41.968 --> 00:00:44.901
and I really want to, like --
you to come see it with me."

00:00:44.901 --> 00:00:48.434
And I think
what he texted back was,

00:00:48.434 --> 00:00:50.300
"Why would I want to see it
with you?"

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.567
[ Audience aws ]
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:00:51.567 --> 00:00:54.534
-I was like,
"Wow! Whoa! Whoa!"

00:00:54.534 --> 00:00:56.367
-Yes. Yeah.
-And I think what he meant was,

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:58.133
"I want to see it with my
friends -- like, you're a mom."

00:00:58.133 --> 00:00:59.701
-"Yeah, I don't go to 'Star' --

00:00:59.701 --> 00:01:01.334
I'm already gonna go see it
with my friends, but..."

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:04.501
-Yeah.
And we did eventually get to --

00:01:04.501 --> 00:01:07.200
We got a huge group together.
We all saw it together.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.367
And they all cheered when I --

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:09.634
It was great.
It was super cool.

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:10.868
-See, that's a moment
that I think

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:12.534
that I'm very lucky
to be able to experience.

00:01:12.534 --> 00:01:13.767
If you go see a movie that's --

00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:15.234
with someone
that's in the movie?

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:16.501
-Yeah.
-I mean...

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:17.767
-I know.
-Dude, it's almost --

00:01:17.767 --> 00:01:18.968
It's, like, emotional.
-It is. You're like...

00:01:18.968 --> 00:01:20.634
-'Cause you're like --
[ Both shouting ]

00:01:20.634 --> 00:01:21.934
-Yeah, I know. "Whoo!"
-And you're --

00:01:21.934 --> 00:01:23.100
Oh, and you're screaming,

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.434
and everyone's like
"Why are they screaming?"

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:25.934
Like, it's just so much --
But it's a good moment.

00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:27.200
-It is super fun.
Yeah, it's really fun.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:29.033
-Yeah, and it's Mom, come on.
-It's Mom. I know.

00:01:29.033 --> 00:01:30.400
-Yeah.
-But I -- It doesn't bug me.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.501
Like, I think that's cool that,
no matter what you do,

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:35.367
you're still an annoying mom
to them.

00:01:35.367 --> 00:01:36.234
[ Laughter ]
-No, never.

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:37.400
-They're like,

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:38.501
"Ohh, you're not that cool."
-No, no.

00:01:38.501 --> 00:01:40.467
We decorated our set
for Halloween.

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:42.067
-Yeah. Oh, yeah.
-Well, these have been here.

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:43.267
These are -- Not these,
but everything else...

00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:44.567
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:44.567 --> 00:01:45.734
-...is Halloween decorated.

00:01:45.734 --> 00:01:47.200
-Well, I really like
the misty nightscape.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.734
-Yeah. That's new.
That's a new addition.

00:01:48.734 --> 00:01:49.968
-Yeah. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:49.968 --> 00:01:51.200
Misty nightscape's a new --
-Misty nightscape.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:52.334
I like a lot.
-You do like it?

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:53.434
-Ooh, I like it.
-Are you --

00:01:53.434 --> 00:01:55.167
Do you dress up for Halloween?
Or...

00:01:55.167 --> 00:01:56.701
-I grew up with a mom who --

00:01:56.701 --> 00:01:59.934
like, she loves Halloween
more than Christmas.

00:01:59.934 --> 00:02:01.334
-Wow.
-She's like, very witchy,

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:04.234
and, like, sends me, you know,
like, "Happy full moon."

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:05.467
You know, like...
-Yeah, I love that.

00:02:05.467 --> 00:02:07.601
-..."Happy Autumn Equinox."
-Yes, yes.

00:02:07.601 --> 00:02:09.501
[ Laughs ]
Exactly, I love that.

00:02:09.501 --> 00:02:11.501
-So, Halloween was a big deal.

00:02:11.501 --> 00:02:13.400
Yeah, the kids will totally
dress up.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.434
My 5-year-old
is being Darth Vader.

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:17.634
-[ Gasps ] What?
-Yeah.

00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:20.934
And with a -- he has this
really cool, like, little thing

00:02:20.934 --> 00:02:24.334
that he pushes, and it says,
like, "Luke, I am your father."

00:02:24.334 --> 00:02:25.667
[ Laughter ]
And then the

00:02:25.667 --> 00:02:29.367
14-year-old is, like,
you know, too cool already.

00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:30.767
He's, like, skateboarding
with his friends.

00:02:30.767 --> 00:02:31.901
He's like "I don't
trick-or-treat."

00:02:31.901 --> 00:02:33.434
-Yeah. I -- when I grew up,
my -- when we --

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:35.267
first off, my kids
are now 6 and 8.

00:02:35.267 --> 00:02:36.334
But when they're first born,

00:02:36.334 --> 00:02:37.501
you can make them
whatever you want.

00:02:37.501 --> 00:02:39.067
-It's the best. It's the best!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.067 --> 00:02:40.200
And they're like...
-That's the greatest.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.467
-It's the best.
They can do whatev--

00:02:41.467 --> 00:02:43.634
Yes. Yes.
-So my -- my --

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:45.000
Winnie was...
-Winnie.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.868
-...they were both
ramen noodle soup once.

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:48.300
[ Laughter ]
-That's so good.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.033
-And I loved that costume.
I said -- And it was just --

00:02:50.033 --> 00:02:51.968
My wife glued yarn to it...
-Oh, my God.

00:02:51.968 --> 00:02:53.634
-...to a little baby onesie.
-It's so good.

00:02:53.634 --> 00:02:56.634
-And we put felt fried egg,
boiled egg in their hair

00:02:56.634 --> 00:02:57.901
and scallions.

00:02:57.901 --> 00:02:59.367
And we're like,
"Yeah, you're a bowl of ramen."

00:02:59.367 --> 00:03:00.934
-That is...so good.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.934 --> 00:03:02.534
-They would never do that now.
Now they're -- Yeah.

00:03:02.534 --> 00:03:04.434
-You can't get them
to do anything.

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:05.734
-No, no.
-No, it's the worst.

00:03:05.734 --> 00:03:06.868
-And -- But they are kind --
they're getting into

00:03:06.868 --> 00:03:08.634
kind of scary --
they love being scared now.

00:03:08.634 --> 00:03:10.100
-Do they?
-Yeah. They enjoy it.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:12.467
So that's why -- But I mean,
maybe not for "Antlers," but...

00:03:12.467 --> 00:03:14.801
-I'd say probably not "Antlers"
for 6-year-olds.

00:03:14.801 --> 00:03:17.067
-But by the way, I will say
your movie "Antlers,"

00:03:17.067 --> 00:03:18.400
that we're gonna talk about...
-Yeah.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.200
-...not only is it --
of course it's scary and it's --

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.300
but it's beautiful.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.767
-It's really -- It is.

00:03:22.767 --> 00:03:24.400
It's kind of one of my favorite
things about the movie.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:26.968
It's very haunt--
Well, Scott Cooper directed it.

00:03:26.968 --> 00:03:29.067
I was such a big fan
of his work. He did --

00:03:29.067 --> 00:03:30.567
I loved "Crazy Heart"...
-Oh, okay.

00:03:30.567 --> 00:03:31.734
-...and a lot of other movies
he did.

00:03:31.734 --> 00:03:33.634
-Oh, yeah, yeah.
-So, when I heard

00:03:33.634 --> 00:03:36.767
that he was making, like,
his version of a scary movie,

00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:39.033
it's sort of, like,
hauntingly beautiful.

00:03:39.033 --> 00:03:41.834
It's a very kind of elegant
scary movie.

00:03:41.834 --> 00:03:43.300
-Yeah.
-And then it has

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:44.801
Guillermo del Toro creating,
like,

00:03:44.801 --> 00:03:45.934
the master
of all the, like, monsters.

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:47.367
-No, no, I can't even -- No.
-It's so --

00:03:47.367 --> 00:03:49.033
-I almost don't ever want
to meet Guillermo del Toro.

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:50.501
-He is -- Oh, my God.
You have to meet him.

00:03:50.501 --> 00:03:51.801
-It's --
-He's amazing and so --

00:03:51.801 --> 00:03:53.334
-He's 10 levels
above everyone else but...

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:56.400
-He's so alive and interested
and curious about everything.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.501
He's like one of those people --
you know, like J.J. Abrams.

00:03:58.501 --> 00:03:59.934
They're just so...
-Yeah.

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:01.367
-They're, like, using more of
their brain than the rest of us.

00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:02.434
-Than everyone else.
-Yeah.

00:04:02.434 --> 00:04:03.801
Yeah, exactly, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.801 --> 00:04:06.200
Now, we -- I want to set up
the movie for everyone.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:07.868
-Okay.
-How -- How do we do it?

00:04:07.868 --> 00:04:11.300
-Okay. So, it's a --
it's a horror movie.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:14.968
Kind of a spooky, moody,
horror movie, set in Oregon.

00:04:14.968 --> 00:04:18.367
I'm a teacher,
and I get obsessed

00:04:18.367 --> 00:04:21.200
with this student of mine
who is harboring a secret.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:24.534
And then, in trying to save him,
I sort of try to save myself.

00:04:24.534 --> 00:04:26.267
-Here we go.
-Okay.

00:04:26.267 --> 00:04:27.834
-I want to show a clip
from the movie.

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:29.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.100
Here's Keri Russell
in the new movie "Antlers."

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:33.234
Take a look at this!

00:04:33.234 --> 00:04:39.200
-Lucas, did they tell you
at the hospital?

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:40.934
-Tell me what?

00:04:40.934 --> 00:04:43.868
♪♪

00:04:43.868 --> 00:04:45.534
-Your dad died.

00:04:45.534 --> 00:04:49.067
♪♪

00:04:49.067 --> 00:04:50.667
-He's not dead.

00:04:50.667 --> 00:04:52.434
♪♪

00:04:52.434 --> 00:04:54.200
-Yeah, he is, Lucas.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:56.300
♪♪

00:04:56.300 --> 00:05:00.567
My brother Paul --
he found him in your house.

00:05:00.567 --> 00:05:02.234
♪♪

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:03.767
-No.

00:05:03.767 --> 00:05:05.501
That was my old dad.

00:05:05.501 --> 00:05:07.767
The one who was sick and mean.

00:05:07.767 --> 00:05:09.868
♪♪

00:05:09.868 --> 00:05:11.601
My new dad is with Aiden.

00:05:11.601 --> 00:05:14.033
But Aiden doesn't understand.

00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:16.067
And he needs me.

00:05:16.067 --> 00:05:18.567
I just have to feed him,
and he'll love me.

00:05:18.567 --> 00:05:21.367
♪♪

00:05:21.367 --> 00:05:22.734
-What?

00:05:22.734 --> 00:05:24.334
-What?! That --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:24.334 --> 00:05:26.267
No, that kid. Come on.
-Creep City.

00:05:26.267 --> 00:05:28.167
-That -- Come on!
-Creep City!

00:05:28.167 --> 00:05:30.133
-Creep City. I love it.
Keri Russell, everybody!

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:32.634
"Antlers" is in theaters today!
[ Cheers and applause ]

